<comment datatype='string'>The &lt;a href=&quot;/gene?orgid=META&amp;id=G-10356&quot;&gt;phaA&lt;/a&gt; gene of &lt;a href=&quot;/META/NEW-IMAGE?object=TAX-1063&quot;&gt;&lt;i&gt;Cereibacter sphaeroides&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/a&gt; was identified by generating transposon mutants
that were defective in acetate metabolism. 
The disrupted gene was very similar to biosynthetic &amp;beta;-ketothiolase from &lt;a href=&quot;/META/NEW-IMAGE?object=TAX-350&quot;&gt;&lt;i&gt;Zoogloea ramigera&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/a&gt;,
suggesting that it encodes a &lt;a href=&quot;/gene?orgid=META&amp;id=MONOMER-13585&quot;&gt;acetyl-CoA acetyltransferase&lt;/a&gt;.
This functional assignment was verified by the fact that the mutant was able to grow on
&lt;a href=&quot;/compound?orgid=META&amp;id=3-KETOBUTYRATE&quot;&gt;acetoacetate&lt;/a&gt; but not on &lt;a href=&quot;/compound?orgid=META&amp;id=ACET&quot;&gt;acetate&lt;/a&gt; [&lt;a href=&quot;http://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pubmed/16856937&quot;&gt;Alber06&lt;/a&gt;].
&lt;p&gt;
</comment>
